{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The WYZE camera felt relevant because I have used home security cameras and could consider adding coverage for another indoor area.",
    "The Echo Dot offered a plausible addition to my Fire TV setup through voice control, while storage cards and an HDMI cable could support my camera and viewing equipment if a specific need arises."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The tablets shared the Amazon and Alexa connection, but that does not give me a reason to want a separate tablet when my recent activity centers on TV viewing and cameras.",
    "Neither pair of earbuds addressed a current listening need, and the HD Fire TV Stick offered little additional value when I already have a 4K Stick and a Fire TV television."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My use of Fire TV seemed to be taken as interest in other Amazon devices, even when they serve a different purpose.",
    "Owning electronic equipment seemed to be taken as a reason to suggest common accessories, without a clear connection to something I currently need."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "What I already own matters: another streaming device needs a clear additional use, and an older or less capable device is less appealing.",
    "Accessories are only useful when they fit my equipment and a concrete task; I would need to confirm storage compatibility, recording capacity, or cable length before choosing them."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in home cameras and Fire TV, but stretched that interest into devices and accessories without enough attention to their added usefulness."
}"}
